@X0BPATHS
-----
@X03A basic diagram of the path structure is shown below:


      +- \NODE1
\PCB -+- \NODE2
      |
      +- \GEN
      +- \MAIN
      |
      +- \CONF1
      +- \CONF2
 
The \PCB directory contains all .EXE files and utilities partaining to PCBoard.

The node subdirectories are the current directories when PCBOARDM.EXE is run.

The GEN directory contains most ascii/ansi screens, and files for the main
board (conference 0).

The MAIN directory contains most PCBoard System files (users, conferences,
etc.)

CONF1 and CONF2 are directories which would actual have a name which is
derived from the name of the corresponding conference.  These directories
contain all files which partain to the configuration of that conference, just
as the \pcb\gen conference contains files partaining to the main board.

Many default paths in the PCBSetup are indicated as ..\gen\ or ..\main\  .
This is to indicate that the current directory is NODE1 or NODE2.  PCBoard will
back up into the \PCB directory (indicated by the two periods <..>), then go
into the GEN or MAIN directory from there.  This causes a problem if your
current directory is not a directory under the PCB directory.

For example, if your current directory is \PCB, then it will go back one (to
the root directory), and then look for the \GEN or \MAIN directory from there.
It won't find it, and will report an error.

If you would like to make your current directory a directory other than the
\PCB\NODE? directory, then you'll need to change all relative paths (..\) in
the pcbsetup program.




 
